  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Safe and Regular Migration through Social Media and Digital Communication in Algeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over the last few years, there has been an increase in the number of Algerian nationals leaving the country irregularly by sea, trying to reach Europe. IOM will implement a project to contribute to promoting safe and regular migration among Algerian nationals that are prone to migrate. To achieve this objective, IOM will make use of social media and digital communication with a Communication for Development (C4D) approach. This will start from an understanding of the context and people&#x2019;s knowledge, attitudes and practices, to then tackle issues by developing empowering messaging tools, rolling out a targeted communication campaign and evaluating its results. The project will contribute to help migrants make informed choices on safe migration through a participatory process, where digital communication is used to support sustainable social and behavioral change.</narrative>
  </description>
